    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "ALI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " tx = thrombectomy/embolectomy, thrombolysis (systemic or catheter-directed) or bypass surg. A fibrinolytic, esp by intra-arterial cath infusion, = most effective for occlusions < 2 wks old w intact motor and sensory funct (a salvageable limb); tPA = most commonly used."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Catheter-directed:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " given @ a rate suited to the pt's size and the extent of thrombosis, USU for 4–24 hrs depending on ischemia severity and signs of thrombolysis."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Interactions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " other drugs that impair hemostasis raise the bleed risk; in ACS, GP IIb/IIIa inhibitors are ⍉recommended for pts receiving fibrinolytics."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "⍉IM injections and monitor for bleed; cholest embolization has been reported, so investigate any new embolic event."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
